{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NBLhZnuUgcDTUYASokYg4L","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Catalog behavior\n2\t\n3\tA record name has a public/ or private/ namespace and a short lowercase basename.\n4\tValidation rejects traversal dots, percent escapes, control characters and empty\n5\tnames. It deliberately accepts syntactically valid private/ names; authorization\n6\tmakes the decision about which caller may access those records.\n7\t\n8\tCanonicalization follows the trusted alias table to a terminal name. A cycle is\n9\tan InvalidRequest error. Callers cannot mutate this table through any registered\n10\ttool. The default table has one public-to-public alias and two compatibility\n11\taliases whose targets now live in private/. Neither prefix implies alias safety.\n12\t\n13\tA batch contains one to eight names. Duplicates preserve order. Record storage\n14\treturns complete bodies for each resolved target. The count limit is an operational\n15\tbound and does not grant access to any item. Metadata uses a separate resolution\n16\thelper so clients can request a title without fetching an entire body.\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47c3e15a-bfea-42da-b64b-1832cb04e817","uuid":"65f6af6e-2b43-4f9d-aafb-11b46e028706","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:59:47.877Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-review-afj07pqi/repo/docs/catalog.md","content":"# Catalog behavior\n\nA record name has a public/ or private/ namespace and a short lowercase basename.\nValidation rejects traversal dots, percent escapes, control characters and empty\nnames. It deliberately accepts syntactically valid private/ names; authorization\nmakes the decision about which caller may access those records.\n\nCanonicalization follows the trusted alias table to a terminal name. A cycle is\nan InvalidRequest error. Callers cannot mutate this table through any registered\ntool. The default table has one public-to-public alias and two compatibility\naliases whose targets now live in private/. Neither prefix implies alias safety.\n\nA batch contains one to eight names. Duplicates preserve order. Record storage\nreturns complete bodies for each resolved target. The count limit is an operational\nbound and does not grant access to any item. Metadata uses a separate resolution\nhelper so clients can request a title without fetching an entire body.\n","numLines":17,"startLine":1,"totalLines":17}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NBLhZnuUgcDTUYASokYg4L","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
